INSERT INTO `assistant_conversations` VALUES (1,3,'explain limits with an example','Unit 1: Relations and Functions 30 Let 𝑓: 𝑅→𝑅  given by  𝑓( ) = 3 + 5. Solution:   \nLet   1,  2 ∈𝑅, 𝑓( 1) = 𝑓( 2) implies  3 1 + 5 = 3 2 + 5 implies  1 =  2 \nTherefore, 𝑓 is one-to-one. In figure 1.16, which of the following sets of values represent a one-to-one function?\n\nKey formulas:\n• Unit 1: Relations and Functions 30 Let 𝑓: 𝑅→𝑅  given by  𝑓( ) = 3 + 5. Show that 𝑓 is one-to-one.\n• Unit 1: Relations and Functions 22 Consider 𝑓( ) = 3 + 4. Find the domain and the range of the function 𝑓.\n• Since 𝑓( ) = 3 + 4 is defined for every real number  , the domain of the function is\n\nExample from your textbook:\nUnit 1: Relations and Functions 30 Let 𝑓: 𝑅→𝑅  given by  𝑓( ) = 3 + 5. Show that 𝑓 is one-to-one.','grade10_math.pdf, page 39','2026-05-21 17:46:06'),(2,3,'thanks','Unit 1: Relations and Functions 54 \nGraphical method of solving quadratic equations In general, the graph of quadratic function has u-shaped curve and one extreme point, \ncalled vertex. In the Activity, the vertex of the function is (0, 0). In order to find the \nsolutions of a quadratic equation using a graph: \n1.\n\nKey formulas:\n• 2. Let 𝑅= {(𝑥, 𝑦): 𝑦 𝑖𝑠 𝑠ℎ𝑜𝑟𝑡𝑒𝑟 𝑡ℎ𝑎𝑛 𝑥}.\n• where 𝑟(𝑥) = 0 or the degree of 𝑟(𝑥) is less than “the degree of 𝑥−𝑐” = 1.\n• But, degree of 𝑟(𝑥) < 1, means “degree of 𝑟(𝑥)” = 0 that is 𝑟(𝑥) is a constant\n• Let 𝑟(𝑥) = 𝑘, since 𝑓(𝑐) = (𝑐−𝑐)𝑞(𝑐) + 𝑟(𝑐) = 0,  𝑟(𝑐) = 0 = 𝑘.\n\nExample from your textbook:\ncalled vertex. In the Activity, the vertex of the function is (0, 0). In order to find the','grade10_math.pdf, page 63','2026-05-21 17:46:18'),(17,2,'Explain limits with an example','Unit 1: Further on Sets If sets 𝐴= {0, 1, 2, 3, 4}  and 𝐵= {3, 4}, then  𝐴−𝐵 or 𝐴\\𝐵= {0, 1, 2}. Let 𝑈 be a universal set of the set of one-digit numbers, 𝐴 be the set of even \nnumbers, 𝐵 be the set of prime numbers less than 10. 𝑈−ሺ𝐴∪𝐵ሻ  or  𝑈\\ሺ𝐴∪𝐵ሻ \nSolution:  \nHere, 𝐴= {0, 2, 4, 6, 8}, 𝐵= {2, 3, 5, 7}.\n\nKey formulas:\n• Here, 𝐴= {0, 2, 4, 6, 8}, 𝐵= {2, 3, 5, 7}.   Then,\n• d. 𝑈−ሺ𝐴∪𝐵ሻ= {1, 9} For the same sets in Example 2, find the following.  What can you say from Example\n• From a. and b., we can say, 𝐴′ = 𝑈−𝐴. From d. and Example 2, a., we can say,\n• a. 𝑥+ 𝑦= 5√3 + 2√2 + √2 −4√3\n\nWorked example from your textbook:\nd. 𝑈−ሺ𝐴∪𝐵ሻ= {1, 9} For the same sets in Example 2, find the following.  What can you say from Example 2 a. and b.?  What about d. and Example 2, a.? a. 𝐴′ b.   𝑈−𝐴 c.    𝐵′ d.   𝐴∩𝐵′ Solution: a. 𝐴′ = {1, 3, 5, 7, 9} b.   𝑈−𝐴= {1, 3, 5, 7, 9} c.   𝐵′ = {0, 1, 4, 6, 8, 9} d.   𝐴∩𝐵′ = {0, 4, 6, 8} From a. and b., we can say, 𝐴′ = 𝑈−𝐴. From d. and Example 2, a., we can say,\n\nWould you like to practice a similar problem?','Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 28 — Unit 1: Further on Sets If sets 𝐴= {0, 1, 2, 3, 4}  and 𝐵= {3, 4}, then  𝐴−𝐵 or 𝐴\\𝐵= {0, 1, 2}. Let 𝑈 be a universal set of the set of one-digit numbers, 𝐴 be the set of even','2026-05-22 08:52:32'),(18,2,'hey','👋 Hello! I\'m your EDUCARE Math Assistant. I\'m here to help you with Grade 9-12 mathematics from your textbooks. What math topic would you like to study today?','','2026-05-22 08:52:37'),(19,2,'how are you','I\'m doing great, thank you for asking! 😊 I\'m ready to help you with any math problems from your textbooks. What would you like to learn today?','','2026-05-22 08:52:41'),(20,4,'Find lim(x→2) (x²-4)/(x-2)','Unit 2: The Number System Rounding \nRounding off is a type of estimation. Estimation is used in everyday life and also in \nsubjects like Mathematics and Physics. Many physical quantities like the amount of \nmoney, distance covered, length measured, etc., are estimated by rounding off the \nactual number to the nearest possible whole number and for decimals at various places \nof hundreds, tens, tenths, etc.\n\nKey formulas:\n• 𝑥+ 2 + ሺ−2ሻ= 0 + ሺ−2ሻ\n• b. Similarly,   3𝑥+ 4 −4 = 10 −4\n• 3 = 2.  Hence,  𝑥= 2 Definition 3.1\n• equation in one variable. It is of the form 𝑎𝑥+ 𝑏= 0, where 𝑥 is the variable,\n\nWorked example from your textbook:\nmy original number? Example Exercise 3.6 118\n\nWould you like to practice a similar problem?','Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 93 — Unit 2: The Number System Rounding','2026-05-22 09:15:34'),(21,4,'hey','👋 Hello! I\'m your EDUCARE Math Assistant. I\'m here to help you with Grade 9-12 mathematics from your textbooks. What math topic would you like to study today?','','2026-05-23 23:12:50'),(22,3,'hey','👋 Hello! I\'m your EDUCARE Math Assistant. I\'m here to help you with Grade 9-12 mathematics from your textbooks. What math topic would you like to study today?','','2026-05-24 09:13:15'),(23,4,'h','I searched the curriculum for your question. Try asking about a specific topic (e.g. quadratic equations, limits, or probability) for a more detailed explanation.','Curriculum — h','2026-05-24 14:22:52'),(24,4,'quadratic equation','I searched the curriculum for your question. Try asking about a specific topic (e.g. quadratic equations, limits, or probability) for a more detailed explanation.','Curriculum — quadratic equation','2026-05-24 14:23:04'),(35,21,'hi','👋 Hello! I\'m your EDUCARE Math Assistant. I\'m here to help you with Grade 9-12 mathematics from your textbooks. What math topic would you like to study today?','','2026-05-25 15:02:38'),(36,21,'what is function','Unit 1: Relations and Functions 31 \nThe set 𝑔( ), shows a different number of elements on each side. This alone will tell \nus that the function is not a one-to-one function. Some values from the left side correspond to the same element found on the right, so \n𝑚( ) is not a one-to-one function as well.\n\nKey formulas:\n• Let  𝑈= {1, 2, 3, … , 10} be a universal set,\n• 𝐴= {𝑥 | 𝑥 is a positive factor of 10 in 𝑈} and\n• 𝐵= {𝑥 | 𝑥 is an odd integer in 𝑈} be sets.\n• Solution: a. 𝐴= {1, 2, 5, 10},  𝐵= {1, 3, 5, 7, 9},  Thus,\n\nExample from your textbook:\nb. Find ሺ𝐴∪𝐵ሻ′ and 𝐴′ ∩𝐵′.  What do you observe from the answers?\n\nWould you like to practice a similar problem?','Ethiopian Grade 10 Mathematics Textbook, page 40 — Unit 1: Relations and Functions 31','2026-05-25 15:02:45'),(37,21,'what is integration','Unit 2: Polynomial Functions 79 \nc. Is the degree of 𝑓∙𝑔 equal to the sum of the degrees of 𝑓 and 𝑔? 𝑓(𝑥) ∙𝑔(𝑥)  = (2𝑥+ 3)( 3𝑥2 −5𝑥+ 6) \n                 = 2𝑥( 3𝑥2 −5𝑥+ 6) + 3( 3𝑥2 −5𝑥+ 6)  (Distributive property) \n                 = ( 2𝑥)(3𝑥2) + (2𝑥)(−5𝑥) + (2𝑥)(6) + (3)(3𝑥2) + (3)(−5𝑥) + (3)(6)          \n                       (Distributive property)                                         \n                  = 6𝑥3 −10𝑥2 + 12𝑥+ 9𝑥2 −15𝑥+ 18 \n                  = 6𝑥3 + (−10𝑥2 + 9𝑥2) + (12𝑥−15𝑥) + 18 \n                  = 6𝑥3 −𝑥2 −3𝑥+ 18 \n    2.\n\nKey formulas:\n• 1.    𝑓(𝑥) ∙𝑔(𝑥)  = (2𝑥+ 3)( 3𝑥2 −5𝑥+ 6)\n• = 2𝑥( 3𝑥2 −5𝑥+ 6) + 3( 3𝑥2 −5𝑥+ 6)  (Distributive property)\n• = ( 2𝑥)(3𝑥2) + (2𝑥)(−5𝑥) + (2𝑥)(6) + (3)(3𝑥2) + (3)(−5𝑥) + (3)(6)\n• = 6𝑥3 −10𝑥2 + 12𝑥+ 9𝑥2 −15𝑥+ 18\n\nWorked example from your textbook:\nc. 180, 270, 1,080 Example 2 Exercise 2.6 41\n\nWould you like to practice a similar problem?','Ethiopian Grade 10 Mathematics Textbook, page 88 — Unit 2: Polynomial Functions 79','2026-05-25 15:02:54'),(38,58,'hi','👋 Hello! I\'m your EDUCARE Math Assistant. I\'m here to help you with Grade 9-12 mathematics from your textbooks. What math topic would you like to study today?','','2026-05-26 10:26:34'),(39,58,'what is the capital city of ethiopia','I\'m sorry, I can only help with Grade 9-12 mathematics from your textbooks.\n\nI can help you with:\n• Algebra\n• Limits\n• Derivatives\n• Integration\n• Word problems\n\nPlease ask a math question from your studies!','','2026-05-26 10:26:47'),(40,58,'help me with algebra','I can help you with:\n\n• Algebra (linear equations, quadratics, functions, factoring)\n• Limits and continuity\n• Derivatives and calculus\n• Integration (definite, indefinite, by parts)\n• Matrices and determinants\n• Vectors\n• Trigonometry\n• Probability and statistics\n• Word problems (age, mixture, work, motion)\n\nJust ask me any math question from your Grade 9-12 textbooks!','','2026-05-26 10:26:55'),(41,58,'what is algebra','Unit 1 Sequences and Series \n31 Solution \nThe nth rectangle has unit length \nand height 2−n units. Hence, the \narea of the nth rectangle is An = 2−n \nsquare unit. =\nr\nr\nr\nr  \n6  \nSuppose a ball is dropped from a height of h m and always rebounds to r of the \nheight from which it falls.\n\nKey formulas:\n• area of the nth rectangle is An = 2−n\n• square units = 1 unit square.\n• From this, by squaring both sides, you get (x − h)2 + (y − k)2 = r2\n• If the centre of a circle is at the origin (i.e. h = 0, k = 0), then the above equation\n\nWorked example from your textbook:\nExample 2  Write down the standard form of the equation of a circle with the given centre and radius. a C (0, 0), r = 8 b C (2, –7), r = 9 Solution a h = k = 0 and r = 8 Therefore, the equation of the circle is (x − 0)2 + (y − 0)2 = 82.\n\nWould you like to practice a similar problem?','Ethiopian Grade 12 Mathematics Textbook, page 39','2026-05-26 10:27:01'),(42,48,'hi','👋 Hello! I\'m your EDUCARE Math Assistant. I\'m here to help you with Grade 9-12 mathematics from your textbooks. What math topic would you like to study today?','','2026-05-26 11:36:21'),(43,48,'how to solve 2x+2=4','Step 1: Isolate the x term.\nStep 2: Simplify to get x = 1.\nAnswer: x = 1','Extreme Mathematics: Grade 9 & 10 (Ethiopia MOE), Chapter 2: Linear Equations','2026-05-26 11:36:30'),(44,48,'how to factorize x^2-1','Step 1: Identify coefficients: a = 1, b = 0, c = -1\nStep 2: Calculate the discriminant Δ = b² - 4ac\n        Δ = 0² - 4×1×-1 = 0 - -4 = 4\nStep 3: x = (-b ± √Δ) / 2a\n        x = (-(0) ± √4) / 2\n        x = (-(0) ± 2.0) / 2\n        x₁ = (2.0) / 2 = 1\n        x₂ = (-2.0) / 2 = -1\nAnswer: x = 1 or x = -1','Extreme Mathematics: Grade 9 & 10 (Ethiopia MOE), Chapter 3: Quadratic Equations','2026-05-26 11:36:59'),(45,48,'what is limit','I\'m sorry — that\'s out of my scope right now. I\'m still under development.\n\nPlease ask something else from your Grade 9–12 math textbooks, such as:\n• Solving linear or quadratic equations\n• Factoring and simplifying expressions\n• Limits, derivatives, or integration\n• Word problems (age, mixture, motion, work)','','2026-05-26 11:37:17'),(46,48,'what is the derivation of 3x^2','I\'m sorry — that\'s out of my scope right now. I\'m still under development.\n\nPlease ask something else from your Grade 9–12 math textbooks, such as:\n• Solving linear or quadratic equations\n• Factoring and simplifying expressions\n• Limits, derivatives, or integration\n• Word problems (age, mixture, motion, work)','','2026-05-26 11:37:59'),(47,48,'how to solve 5x-2=1','Step 1: Isolate the x term.\nStep 2: Simplify to get x = 0.6.\nAnswer: x = 0.6','Extreme Mathematics: Grade 9 & 10 (Ethiopia MOE), Chapter 2: Linear Equations','2026-05-26 11:39:46'),(48,48,'hello','👋 Hello! I\'m your EDUCARE Math Assistant. I\'m here to help you with Grade 9-12 mathematics from your textbooks. What math topic would you like to study today?','','2026-05-26 11:40:04'),(49,58,'lim(x→0) sin(x)/x → 1','Step 1: Substitute x = 0 directly into the expression.\nStep 2: Evaluate f(0) = 0.\nAnswer: 0','Ethiopian Grade 12 Mathematics Textbook — Limits and Continuity','2026-05-26 11:42:45'),(50,58,'what is probablity','I\'m sorry — that\'s out of my scope right now. I\'m still under development.\n\nPlease ask something else from your Grade 9–12 math textbooks, such as:\n• Solving linear or quadratic equations\n• Factoring and simplifying expressions\n• Limits, derivatives, or integration\n• Word problems (age, mixture, motion, work)','','2026-05-26 11:43:14'),(51,58,'how to factorize x^2','I\'m sorry — that\'s out of my scope right now. I\'m still under development.\n\nPlease ask something else from your Grade 9–12 math textbooks, such as:\n• Solving linear or quadratic equations\n• Factoring and simplifying expressions\n• Limits, derivatives, or integration\n• Word problems (age, mixture, motion, work)','','2026-05-26 11:45:52'),(52,58,'how to solve 2x + 2=1','Step 1: Isolate the x term.\nStep 2: Simplify to get x = -0.5.\nAnswer: x = -0.5','Extreme Mathematics: Grade 9 & 10 (Ethiopia MOE), Chapter 2: Linear Equations','2026-05-26 11:46:04'),(53,58,'how to factorize x^3-2+1','I\'m sorry — that\'s out of my scope right now. I\'m still under development.\n\nPlease ask something else from your Grade 9–12 math textbooks, such as:\n• Solving linear or quadratic equations\n• Factoring and simplifying expressions\n• Limits, derivatives, or integration\n• Word problems (age, mixture, motion, work)','','2026-05-26 11:46:23'),(54,58,'how to factorize x^2-1','I\'m sorry — that\'s out of my scope right now. I\'m still under development.\n\nPlease ask something else from your Grade 9–12 math textbooks, such as:\n• Solving linear or quadratic equations\n• Factoring and simplifying expressions\n• Limits, derivatives, or integration\n• Word problems (age, mixture, motion, work)','','2026-05-26 11:46:46'),(55,58,'simplify x3+x','I\'m sorry — that\'s out of my scope right now. I\'m still under development.\n\nPlease ask something else from your Grade 9–12 math textbooks, such as:\n• Solving linear or quadratic equations\n• Factoring and simplifying expressions\n• Limits, derivatives, or integration\n• Word problems (age, mixture, motion, work)','','2026-05-26 11:47:02'),(56,58,'find the derivative of 3x² + 2x - 5','Step 1: Apply the power rule d/dx[x^n] = n·x^(n-1) term by term:\n  • d/dx[3x²] = 6x\n  • d/dx[2x] = 2\n  • d/dx[-5.0] = 0\nStep 2: Combine the terms.\nAnswer: 6x+2','Ethiopian Grade 12 Mathematics Textbook — Introduction to Differential Calculus','2026-05-26 11:47:18'),(57,41,'hi','👋 Hello! I\'m your EDUCARE Math Assistant. I\'m here to help you with Grade 9-12 mathematics from your textbooks. What math topic would you like to study today?','','2026-05-26 12:16:02'),(58,41,'how to solve 3x-2=1','Step 1: Isolate the x term.\nStep 2: Simplify to get x = 1.\nAnswer: x = 1','Extreme Mathematics: Grade 9 & 10 (Ethiopia MOE), Chapter 2: Linear Equations','2026-05-26 12:16:16'),(59,41,'what is the derivation of 3x^2+2x','Step 1: Apply the power rule d/dx[x^n] = n·x^(n-1) term by term:\n  • d/dx[3x²] = 6x\n  • d/dx[2x] = 2\nStep 2: Combine the terms.\nAnswer: 6x+2','Ethiopian Grade 12 Mathematics Textbook — Introduction to Differential Calculus','2026-05-26 12:16:47'),(68,63,'solve 3x010','I\'m sorry — that\'s out of my scope right now. I\'m still under development.\n\nPlease ask something else from your Grade 9–12 math textbooks, such as:\n• Solving linear or quadratic equations\n• Factoring and simplifying expressions\n• Limits, derivatives, or integration\n• Word problems (age, mixture, motion, work)','','2026-05-28 07:48:34'),(69,63,'how to solve 3x-5=6','Step 1: Isolate the x term.\nStep 2: Simplify to get x = 3.6667.\nAnswer: x = 3.6667','Extreme Mathematics: Grade 9 & 10 (Ethiopia MOE), Chapter 2: Linear Equations','2026-05-28 08:12:35'),(70,63,'what is the capital city of ethiopia','I\'m sorry — that\'s out of my scope right now. I\'m still under development.\n\nPlease ask something else from your Grade 9–12 math textbooks, such as:\n• Solving linear or quadratic equations\n• Factoring and simplifying expressions\n• Limits, derivatives, or integration\n• Word problems (age, mixture, motion, work)','','2026-05-28 08:13:26'),(71,63,'how to solve 2x^2+4=0','Step 1: Identify coefficients: a = 2, b = 0, c = 4\nStep 2: Calculate the discriminant Δ = b² - 4ac\n        Δ = 0² - 4×2×4 = 0 - 32 = -32\nSince Δ < 0, the roots are complex (no real solution).','Extreme Mathematics: Grade 9 & 10 (Ethiopia MOE), Chapter 3: Quadratic Equations','2026-05-28 08:46:39'),(72,63,'how to solve x^2-9x+14=0','Step 1: Identify coefficients: a = 1, b = -9, c = 14\nStep 2: Calculate the discriminant Δ = b² - 4ac\n        Δ = -9² - 4×1×14 = 81 - 56 = 25\nStep 3: x = (-b ± √Δ) / 2a\n        x = (-(-9) ± √25) / 2\n        x = (-(-9) ± 5.0) / 2\n        x₁ = (14.0) / 2 = 7\n        x₂ = (4.0) / 2 = 2\nAnswer: x = 7 or x = 2','Extreme Mathematics: Grade 9 & 10 (Ethiopia MOE), Chapter 3: Quadratic Equations','2026-05-28 08:47:33'),(73,63,'how to solve x^2=4','Step 1: Identify coefficients: a = 1, b = 0, c = 0\nStep 2: Calculate the discriminant Δ = b² - 4ac\n        Δ = 0² - 4×1×0 = 0 - 0 = 0\nStep 3: x = -b / (2a) = -(0) / (2×1) = 0\nAnswer: x = 0 (repeated/double root)','Extreme Mathematics: Grade 9 & 10 (Ethiopia MOE), Chapter 3: Quadratic Equations','2026-05-28 08:48:07');
