questions\"><h3>Practice Questions</h3><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"0\"><p><strong>Q1.</strong> Find the roots of:  x² - 2x + 1 = 0</p><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. x = 1 (double root)</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. x = 2 and x = 2</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. x = -1 and x = -1</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. x = 1 and x = 2</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: A</strong> — Factor: (x - 1)(x - 1) = 0  →  x = 1 or x = 1</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"1\"><p><strong>Q2.</strong> Solve the system:  x + y = 4  and  x - y = -2</p><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. x = 3, y = 1</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. x = 1, y = 3</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. x = 2, y = 2</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. x = 4, y = -2</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: B</strong> — Add equations: 2x = 2  →  x = 1;  then y = 4 - 1 = 3</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"2\"><p><strong>Q3.</strong> Solve for x:  x + 1 = 22</p><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 24</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 18</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 21</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 19</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: C</strong> — Subtract 1 from both sides: x = 22 - 1 = 21</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"0\"><p><strong>Q4.</strong> Solve for x:  x + 2 = 7</p><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 5</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 8</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 3</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 6</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: A</strong> — Subtract 2 from both sides: x = 7 - 2 = 5</div></div></div>','grade10_math.pdf, page 23','Approved','2026-04-09 00:41:59',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0),(12,3,'Practice: Integration','<div class=\"rag-explanation\"><h3>Curriculum Overview</h3><p>Hence, points above the line  =    \nare  members of the relation 𝑅. Sketch the graph of the relation 𝑅 if 𝑅 be the set of ordered pairs ( ,  ) of real \nnumbers   and    such that  ≤ + 2.</p></div>\n<div class=\"rag-formulas\"><h3>Key Formulas</h3><ul><li><code>below the line  =  .</code></li><li><code>4. The ordered pair (0, 3) satisfies the relation. Hence, points above the line  =</code></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"rag-examples\"><h3>Curriculum Examples</h3><ul><li>Example 4 Figure 1.8 the graph of the relation  ≤ + 2.</li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"rag-questions\"><h3>Practice Questions</h3><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"2\"><p><strong>Q1.</strong> Find:  ∫ 8 dx</p><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 8x²/2 + C</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 9x + C</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 8x + C</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 7x + C</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: C</strong> — ∫ constant dx = constant·x + C  →  ∫ 8 dx = 8x + C</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"2\"><p><strong>Q2.</strong> Find:  ∫ 7x^4 dx</p><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. (7)x^5 + C</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. (7/5)x^4 + C</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. (7/5)x^5 + C</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. (28)x^3 + C</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: C</strong> — Power rule: ∫ ax^n dx = a·x^(n+1)/(n+1) + C = (7/5)x^5 + C = 7/5x^5 + C</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"3\"><p><strong>Q3.</strong> Find:  ∫ 11 dx</p><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 11x²/2 + C</li><li data-idx=\"1\