tion\" data-correct=\"0\"><p><strong>Q3.</strong> Find:  ∫ (6x + 3) dx</p><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. (3)x² + 3x + C</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. (6)x² + 3x + C</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. (3)x² + 4x + C</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 6 + C</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: A</strong> — Integrate term by term: 6x²/2 + 3x + C = 3x² + 3x + C</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"1\"><p><strong>Q4.</strong> Evaluate:  ∫₀^3 x dx</p><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 3</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 9/2</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 9</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 5</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: B</strong> — ∫ x dx = x²/2  →  [3²/2 - 0²/2] = 9/2 = 9/2</div></div></div>','grade10_math.pdf, page 23','Approved','2026-05-20 20:48:28',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0),(16,3,'Practice: Integration','<div class=\"rag-explanation\"><h3>Curriculum Overview</h3><p>Hence, points above the line  =    \nare  members of the relation 𝑅. Sketch the graph of the relation 𝑅 if 𝑅 be the set of ordered pairs ( ,  ) of real \nnumbers   and    such that  ≤ + 2.</p></div>\n<div class=\"rag-formulas\"><h3>Key Formulas</h3><ul><li><code>below the line  =  .</code></li><li><code>4. The ordered pair (0, 3) satisfies the relation. Hence, points above the line  =</code></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"rag-examples\"><h3>Curriculum Examples</h3><ul><li>Example 4 Figure 1.8 the graph of the relation  ≤ + 2.</li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"rag-questions\"><h3>Practice Questions</h3><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"0\"><p><strong>Q1.</strong> Evaluate:  ∫₀^2 x dx</p><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 2</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 2</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 4</li><l