om both sides: x = 28 - 13 = 15</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"1\"><p><strong>Q4.</strong> Find the roots of:  x² - 5x + 4 = 0</p><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. x = 2 and x = 5</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. x = 1 and x = 4</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. x = -1 and x = -4</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. x = 4 and x = 5</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: B</strong> — Factor: (x - 1)(x - 4) = 0  →  x = 1 or x = 4</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"0\"><p><strong>Q5.</strong> Solve for x:  5x = 15</p><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 3</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 2</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 4</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 8</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: A</strong> — Divide both sides by 5: x = 15 / 5 = 3</div></div></div>','grade10_math.pdf, page 23','Approved','2026-05-21 11:41:14','grade10_math',3,10,0,0),(21,2,'Practice: Limits','<div class=\"rag-explanation\"><h3>Curriculum Overview</h3><p>Unit 1: Relations and Functions 54 \nGraphical method of solving quadratic equations In general, the graph of quadratic function has u-shaped curve and one extreme point, \ncalled vertex. In the Activity, the vertex of the function is (0, 0). In order to find the \nsolutions of a quadratic equation using a graph: \n1.</p></div>\n<div class=\"rag-formulas\"><h3>Key Formulas</h3><ul><li><code>= 𝑎 2 + 𝑏 + 𝑐 = 𝑎 ( +</code></li><li><code>4𝑎2 = 𝑎 ( +</code></li><li><code>= 𝑎 ( +</code></li><li><code>(That is, translate  = 𝑎 2 by −</code></li><li><code>2. Let 𝑅= {(𝑥, 𝑦): 𝑦 𝑖𝑠 𝑠ℎ𝑜𝑟𝑡𝑒𝑟 𝑡ℎ𝑎𝑛 𝑥}.</code></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"rag-examples\"><h3>Curriculum Examples</h3><ul><li>called vertex. In the Activity, the vertex of the function is (0, 0). In order to find the</li><li>3. Find the domain and range of each of the following relations:</li><li>4. Sketch the graph of each of the following relations and find the domain and range.</li><li>𝑓(𝑐) = (𝑐−𝑐)𝑞(𝑥) = 0. a.   Show that 𝑥+ 2 is a factor of 𝑓(𝑥) =  𝑥2 + 5𝑥+ 6.</li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"rag-questions\"><h3>Practice Questions</h3><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"2\"><p><strong>Q1.</strong> Evaluate:  lim(x → ∞)  (5x + 8) / (6x + 8)</p><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 1</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 5/7</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 5/6</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 1</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: C</strong> — Divide numerator and denominator by x: limit = 5/6 = 5/6</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"1\"><p><strong>Q2.</strong> Evaluate:  lim(x → 4)  (x + 4)</p><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 9</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 8</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 10</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 4</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: B</strong> — Direct substitution: 4 + 4 = 8</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"2\"><p><strong>Q3.</strong> Evaluate:  lim(x → 0)  sin(2x) / (2x)</p><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 0</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 2</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 1</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 1/2</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: C</strong> — Using the standard limit lim(u→0) sin(u)/u = 1, with u = 2x, the answer is 1</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"2\"><p><strong>Q4.</strong> Evaluate:  lim(x → ∞)  (2x + 2) / (2x + 6)</p><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 3/2</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 2/3</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 1</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 1/3</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: C</strong> — Divide numerator and denominator by x: limit = 2/2 = 1</div></div></div>','grade10_math.pdf, page 63','Approved','2026-05-21 12:16:56',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0),(22,6,'Function (Grade 9)','<div class=\"rag-questions\"><h3>Practice Questions</h3><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"2\"><p><strong>Q1.</strong> Convert 60° to radians (in terms of π)</p><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. π/4</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. π/6</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. π/3</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 0</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: C</strong> — 60° × (π/180) = 60π/180 = π/3</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"3\"><p><strong>Q2.</strong> Convert 30° to radians (in terms of π)</p><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. π/3</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. π/2</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 0</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. π/6</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: D</strong> — 30° × (π/180) = 30π/180 = π/6</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"0\"><p><strong>Q3.</strong> Convert 45° to radians (in terms of π)</p><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. π/4</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. π/2</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. π</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 0</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: A</strong> — 45° × (π/180) = 45π/180 = π/4</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"0\"><p><strong>Q4.</strong> Find: sin(90°)</p><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 1</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 0</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 1</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 90/180</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: A</strong> — Using the unit circle / special angles table: sin(90°) = 1</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"1\"><p><strong>Q5.</strong> Convert 90° to radians (in terms of π)</p><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. π</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. π/2</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. π/4</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 0</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: B</strong> — 90° × (π/180) = 90π/180 = π/2</div></div></div>','Grade 9 Mathematics Curriculum – Function','Approved','2026-05-21 12:18:14',NULL,NULL,9,0,0),(23,2,'Limit (Grade 12)','<div class=\"rag-questions\"><h3>Practice Questions</h3><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"0\"><p><strong>Q1.</strong> Evaluate:  lim(x → 5)  (x + 10)</p><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 15</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 5</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 10</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 14</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: A</strong> — Direct substitution: 5 + 10 = 15</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"2\"><p><strong>Q2.</strong> Evaluate:  lim(x → ∞)  (3x + 1) / (3x + 6)</p><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 4/3</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 3/4</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 1</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 1/6</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: C</strong> — Divide numerator and denominator by x: limit = 3/3 = 1</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"3\"><p><strong>Q3.</strong> Evaluate:  lim(x → 6)  (x² - 36) / (x - 6)</p><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 11</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 36</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 13</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 12</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: D</strong> — Factor numerator: (x-6)(x+6)/(x-6) = x+6  →  at x=6: 6+6 = 12</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"0\"><p><strong>Q4.</strong> Evaluate:  lim(x → 0)  sin(2x) / (2x)</p><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 1</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 0</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 2</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 1/2</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: A</strong> — Using the standard limit lim(u→0) sin(u)/u = 1, with u = 2x, the answer is 1</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"1\"><p><strong>Q5.</strong> Evaluate:  lim(x → 1)  (x + 9)</p><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 9</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 10</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 11</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 12</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: B</strong> — Direct substitution: 1 + 9 = 10</div></div></div>','Grade 12 Mathematics Curriculum – Limit','Approved','2026-05-21 14:36:17',NULL,NULL,12,0,0),(24,7,'Quadratic Equation (Grade 10)','<div class=\"rag-explanation\"><h3>Curriculum Overview (Grade 10)</h3><p>Unit 1: Relations and Functions 41 \n3. Sketch the graph of each of the following using intercepts: \na. = −4 + 3 Graphs of quadratic functions \nA function defined by 𝑓( ) = 𝑎 2 + 𝑏 + 𝑐 where 𝑎, 𝑏, 𝑐  are real numbers and 𝑎≠\n0 is called a quadratic function.</p></div>\n<div class=\"rag-formulas\"><h3>Key Formulas</h3><ul><li><code>A function defined by 𝑓( ) = 𝑎 2 + 𝑏 + 𝑐 where 𝑎, 𝑏, 𝑐  are real numbers and 𝑎≠</code></li><li><code>Make a table of ordered pairs that satisfy the function  𝑓( ) =  2.</code></li><li><code>2. Graph the function 𝑓( ) = 𝑎 2 + 𝑏 + 𝑐 using properties or transformations.</code></li><li><code>The graph of a quadratic function 𝑓( ) = 𝑎 2 + 𝑏 + 𝑐 is a parabola. When we ask</code></li><li><code>=  2 + 4 + 8 = ( + 2)2 + 4</code></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"rag-examples\"><h3>Curriculum Examples</h3><ul><li>a.  = 2 + 4       𝑏.  3 + 4 = 5         𝑐.    = −4 + 3 Graphs of quadratic functions</li><li>0 is called a quadratic function. The point 𝑎 is the leading coefficient of 𝑓. 𝑓( ) = 3 2 −2 + 5 is a quadratic function with 𝑎= 3, 𝑏= −2 and 𝑐= 5.</li><li>function is not sufficient. For example, the motion of an object thrown either upward or downward is modeled by a quadratic function. The graph of a quadratic function is a curve called a parabola. Parabolas may open upward or downward and vary in” width” or” steepness”, but they all have the same b</li><li>stretching/ shrinking and shifting (translation) the parabola  =  2. Example 1 The simplest form of a quadratic equation is  =  2 when 𝑎 =  1 and 𝑏 =  𝑐 =  0. Note a. Make a table of ordered pairs that satisfy the function  𝑓( ) =  2. b. Find the   and   intercepts of  𝑓.</li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"rag-questions\"><h3>Practice Questions</h3><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"0\"><p><strong>Q1.</strong> Solve the system:  x + y = 6  and  x - y = -4</p><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. x = 1, y = 5</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. x = 5, y = 1</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. x = 2, y = 4</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. x = 6, y = -4</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: A</strong> — Add equations: 2x = 2  →  x = 1;  then y = 6 - 1 = 5</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"3\"><p><strong>Q2.</strong> Solve for x:  x + 6 = 31</p><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 24</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 26</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 27</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 25</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: D</strong> — Subtract 6 from both sides: x = 31 - 6 = 25</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"2\"><p><strong>Q3.</strong> Solve for x:  2x = 18</p><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 8</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 10</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 9</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 11</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: C</strong> — Divide both sides by 2: x = 18 / 2 = 9</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"0\"><p><strong>Q4.</strong> Solve the system:  x + y = 10  and  x - y = -4</p><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. x = 3, y = 7</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. x = 7, y = 3</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. x = 4, y = 6</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. x = 10, y = -4</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: A</strong> — Add equations: 2x = 6  →  x = 3;  then y = 10 - 3 = 7</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"2\"><p><strong>Q5.</strong> Find the roots of:  x² - 13x + 42 = 0</p><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. x = 7 and x = 8</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. x = -6 and x = -7</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. x = 6 and x = 7</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. x = 42 and x = 13</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: C</strong> — Factor: (x - 6)(x - 7) = 0  →  x = 6 or x = 7</div></div></div>','grade10_math.pdf, page 50','Approved','2026-05-21 14:36:42','grade10_math',50,10,0,0),(25,3,'Integration (Grade 10)','<div class=\"rag-explanation\"><h3>Curriculum Ov