" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: D</strong> — ∫ x dx = x²/2  →  [5²/2 - 0²/2] = 25/2 = 25/2</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"0\"><p><strong>Q3.</strong> Find:  ∫ 10 dx</p><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 10x + C</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 10x²/2 + C</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 11x + C</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 9x + C</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: A</strong> — ∫ constant dx = constant·x + C  →  ∫ 10 dx = 10x + C</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"3\"><p><strong>Q4.</strong> Find:  ∫ (5x + 5) dx</p><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. (5)x² + 5x + C</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. (5/2)x² + 6x + C</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 5 + C</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. (5/2)x² + 5x + C</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: D</strong> — Integrate term by term: 5x²/2 + 5x + C = (5/2)x² + 5x + C = 5/2x² + 5x + C</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"2\"><p><strong>Q5.</strong> Find:  ∫ 2x^4 dx</p><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. (2)x^5 + C</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. (2/5)x^4 + C</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. (2/5)x^5 + C</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. (8)x^3 + C</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: C</strong> — Power rule: ∫ ax^n dx = a·x^(n+1)/(n+1) + C = (2/5)x^5 + C = 2/5x^5 + C</div></div></div>','grade10_math.pdf, page 63','Approved','2026-05-21 14:37:39','grade10_math',63,10,0,0),(26,5,'Probablity (Grade 10)','<div class=\"rag-explanation\"><h3>Curriculum Overview (Grade 10)</h3><p>Unit 1: Relations and Functions 54 \nGraphical method of solving quadratic equations In general, the graph of quadratic function has u-shaped curve and on