ay:none\"><strong>Answer: D</strong> — Factor: (x - 4)(x - 4) = 0  →  x = 4 or x = 4</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"3\"><p><strong>Q2.</strong> Find the roots of:  x² - 15x + 56 = 0</p><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. x = 9 and x = 8</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. x = -8 and x = -7</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. x = 56 and x = 15</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. x = 8 and x = 7</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: D</strong> — Factor: (x - 8)(x - 7) = 0  →  x = 8 or x = 7</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"1\"><p><strong>Q3.</strong> Solve the system:  x + y = 17  and  x - y = 3</p><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. x = 7, y = 10</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. x = 10, y = 7</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. x = 11, y = 6</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. x = 17, y = 3</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: B</strong> — Add equations: 2x = 20  →  x = 10;  then y = 17 - 10 = 7</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"3\"><p><strong>Q4.</strong> Solve the system:  x + y = 11  and  x - y = -9</p><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. x = 10, y = 1</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. x = 2, y = 9</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. x = 11, y = -9</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. x = 1, y = 10</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: D</strong> — Add equations: 2x = 2  →  x = 1;  then y = 11 - 1 = 10</div></div></div>','grade10_math.pdf, page 63','Approved','2026-05-22 09:47:14','grade10_math.pdf',63,10,0,0),(30,1,'Practice: Algebra','<div class=\"rag-explanation\"><h3>Curriculum Overview</h3><p>Unit 1: Relations and Functions 54 \nGraphical method of solving quadratic equations In general, the 