Curriculum Examples</h3><ul><li>Unit 3: Solving Equations Activity 3.1 leads you to revise the rules used to solve linear equations that you</li><li>Step 4: Verify your answer. Solve for 𝑥, if</li><li>a.  𝑥+ 2 = 0                                   b.   3𝑥+ 4 = 10</li><li>b. Similarly,   3𝑥+ 4 −4 = 10 −4</li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"rag-questions\"><h3>Practice Questions</h3><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"1\"><p><strong>Q1.</strong> Solve for x:  x + 9 = 20</p><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 8</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 11</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 10</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 12</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: B</strong> — Subtract 9 from both sides: x = 20 - 9 = 11</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"3\"><p><strong>Q2.</strong> Find the roots of:  x² - 12x + 35 = 0</p><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. x = 6 and x = 8</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. x = -5 and x = -7</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. x = 35 and x = 12</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. x = 5 and x = 7</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: D</strong> — Factor: (x - 5)(x - 7) = 0  →  x = 5 or x = 7</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"3\"><p><strong>Q3.</strong> Find the roots of:  x² - 6x + 5 = 0</p><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. x = 6 and x = 2</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. x = -5 and x = -1</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. x = 5 and x = 6</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. x = 5 and x = 1</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: D</strong> — Factor: (x - 5)(x - 1) = 0  →  x = 5 or x = 1</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"1\"><p><strong>Q4.</strong> Solve the system:  x + y 