2\"><p><strong>Q2.</strong> Evaluate:  lim(x → 6)  (x + 1)</p><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Curriculum Source</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 8</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 1</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 7</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 6</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: C</strong> — Direct substitution: 6 + 1 = 7</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"0\"><p><strong>Q3.</strong> Evaluate:  lim(x → 3)  (x² - 9) / (x - 3)</p><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Curriculum Source</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 6</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 9</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 3</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 5</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: A</strong> — Factor numerator: (x-3)(x+3)/(x-3) = x+3  →  at x=3: 3+3 = 6</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"2\"><p><strong>Q4.</strong> Evaluate:  lim(x → 3)  (x + 1)</p><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Curriculum Source</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 1</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 3</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 4</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 5</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: C</strong> — Direct substitution: 3 + 1 = 4</div></div></div>','Extreme Mathematics: Grade 9 & 10 — Unit 4: Trigonometric Function 228','Approved','2026-05-22 15:23:45','Extreme Mathematics Grade 9&10.pdf_page_130.txt',0,NULL,0,0),(41,1,'Practice: Algebra','<div class=\"rag-sources\"><p>ℹ️ Source: <strong>Extreme Mathematics: Grade 9 & 10</strong> – Exam-style questions extracted from this textbook.<br>All 6 curriculum textbooks were searched; Extreme books given priority.</p></div>\n<div class=\"rag-explanation\"><