div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"2\"><p><strong>Q2.</strong> Convert 180° to radians (in terms of π)</p><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Curriculum Source</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. π/2</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 2π</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. π</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 0</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: C</strong> — 180° × (π/180) = 180π/180 = π</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"0\"><p><strong>Q3.</strong> Find: cos(45°)</p><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Curriculum Source</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. √2/2</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 1</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 1/2</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. √3/2</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: A</strong> — Using the unit circle / special angles table: cos(45°) = √2/2</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"1\"><p><strong>Q4.</strong> Convert 30° to radians (in terms of π)</p><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Curriculum Source</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. π/3</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. π/6</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. π/2</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 0</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: B</strong> — 30° × (π/180) = 30π/180 = π/6</div></div></div>','Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 61 — Unit 2: The Number System 2.2.2  Conversion of repeating decimals into fractions','Approved','2026-05-25 10:34:06','grade9_math.pdf',61,NULL,0,0),(59,2,'Practice: limit','<div class=\"rag-explanation\"><h3>Curriculum Overview</h3><p>The difference of a number and 6 is between 0 and  . One plus twice a number is greater than 1and less than 5. One-third of a 