-correct=\"0\"><p><strong>Q3.</strong> Evaluate:  lim(x → ∞)  (5x + 5) / (3x + 8)</p><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Curriculum Source</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 5/3</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 2</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 5/4</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 5/8</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: A</strong> — Divide numerator and denominator by x: limit = 5/3 = 5/3</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"0\"><p><strong>Q4.</strong> Evaluate:  lim(x → 5)  (x + 9)</p><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Curriculum Source</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 14</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 5</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 9</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 13</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: A</strong> — Direct substitution: 5 + 9 = 14</div></div></div>','Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 191 — Unit 4: Solving Inequalities 1. Answer the following questions.','Approved','2026-05-25 10:39:59','grade9_math.pdf',191,NULL,0,0),(60,2,'Practice: limit','<div class=\"rag-explanation\"><h3>Curriculum Overview</h3><p>The difference of a number and 6 is between 0 and  . One plus twice a number is greater than 1and less than 5. One-third of a number is either less than 2 or greater than 5.</p></div>\n<div class=\"rag-formulas\"><h3>Key Formulas</h3><ul><li><code>2 (since 0.5 =</code></li><li><code>b. 5 + (−8 + 2) = (5 −8) + 2</code></li><li><code>defined as 𝑎∗𝑏= 2𝑎+ 𝑏.</code></li><li><code>Unit 3: Solving Equations Factorization Method 2 Solve the quadratic equation 𝑥2 + 6𝑥+ 9 = 0</code></li><li><code>ሺ𝑥+ 3ሻሺ𝑥+ 3ሻ= ሺ𝑥+ 3ሻ2 = 0 (Factorizing: sum = 6  and product = 9).</code></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"rag-examples\"><h3>Curriculum Examples</h3><ul><li>a. The difference of a number and 6 i