-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. x = 24 and x = 11</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: A</strong> — Factor: (x - 8)(x - 3) = 0  →  x = 8 or x = 3</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"0\"><p><strong>Q3.</strong> Solve for x:  5x = 35</p><span class=\"rag-style-tag extreme\">Exam-style from Extreme Mathematics</span><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 61</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 7</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 6</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 40</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 8</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: A</strong> — Divide both sides by 5: x = 35 / 5 = 7</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"1\"><p><strong>Q4.</strong> Solve for x:  9x = 135</p><span class=\"rag-style-tag grade\">Foundational — Grade Textbook</span><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 61</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 14</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 15</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 144</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 16</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: B</strong> — Divide both sides by 9: x = 135 / 9 = 15</div></div></div>','Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 61 — Unit 2: The Number System 2.2.2  Conversion of repeating decimals into fractions','Approved','2026-05-25 11:06:31','grade9_math.pdf',61,NULL,0,0),(71,1,'Practice: Algebra','<div class=\"rag-explanation\"><h3>Curriculum Overview</h3><p>Unit 2: The Number System 2.2.2  Conversion of repeating decimals into fractions \nIn section 2.2.1, you have discussed how to convert the terminating decimals into \nfractions. In this subsection, you will learn how repeating decimals can be converted \nto fraction