> — Subtract 16 from both sides: x = 17 - 16 = 1</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"2\"><p><strong>Q3.</strong> Find the roots of:  x² - 4x + 3 = 0</p><span class=\"rag-style-tag extreme\">Exam-style from Extreme Mathematics</span><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 61</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. x = 4 and x = 2</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. x = -3 and x = -1</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. x = 3 and x = 1</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. x = 3 and x = 4</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: C</strong> — Factor: (x - 3)(x - 1) = 0  →  x = 3 or x = 1</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"0\"><p><strong>Q4.</strong> Solve for x:  x + 9 = 37</p><span class=\"rag-style-tag grade\">Foundational — Grade Textbook</span><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 61</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 28</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 27</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 29</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 30</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: A</strong> — Subtract 9 from both sides: x = 37 - 9 = 28</div></div></div>','Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 61 — Unit 2: The Number System 2.2.2  Conversion of repeating decimals into fractions','Approved','2026-05-25 11:06:32','grade9_math.pdf',61,NULL,0,0),(72,7,'Practice: Quadratic Equation','<div class=\"rag-explanation\"><h3>Curriculum Overview</h3><p>A system of linear equation in two variables can be solved by one of the \nfollowing methods: graphically, or by substitution or by elimination. The absolute value of a number 𝑥, denoted by |𝑥|, is defined as the distance \n|𝑥| from zero on a number line. For any non- negative number 𝑝, |𝑥| = 𝑝  means 𝑥= 𝑝  or 𝑥= −𝑝.</p></div>\n<div class=\"rag-formulas\"><h3>Key Formulas</h3><ul><li><code>9. For any non- negative number 𝑝, |𝑥| = 𝑝  means 𝑥= 𝑝  or 𝑥= −𝑝.</code></li><li><code>10. An equation of the form 𝑎𝑥2 + 𝑏𝑥+ 𝑐= 0  where a, b, c, ∈ R and 𝑎≠0  is a</code></li><li><code>can be used to solve a quadratic equation 𝑎𝑥2 + 𝑏𝑥+ 𝑐= 0</code></li><li><code>12. If the quadratic equation, 𝑎𝑥2 + 𝑏𝑥+ 𝑐= 0, has roots</code></li><li><code>13. The discriminant of quadratic equations, 𝐷= 𝑏2 −4𝑎𝑐,</code></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"rag-examples\"><h3>Worked Examples from Textbook</h3><ul><li>d. 𝑥2 −4𝑥+ 3 = 0 Example 1 Example 2 Exercise 3.10 128</li><li>Example 2  Write down the standard form of the equation of a circle with the given centre and radius. a C (0, 0), r = 8 b C (2, –7), r = 9 Solution a h = k = 0 and r = 8 Therefore, the equation of the circle is (x − 0)2 + (y − 0)2 = 82.</li><li>Example 3  Write the standard form of the equation of the circle with centre at C (2, 3) and that passes through the point P (7, –3). x y P(x, y) r C(h, k) •</li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"rag-questions\"><h3>Practice Questions</h3><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"2\"><p><strong>Q1.</strong> Solve for x:  10x = 90</p><span class=\"rag-style-tag extreme\">Exam-style from Extreme Mathematics</span><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 159</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 100</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 8</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 9</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 10</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: C</strong> — Divide both sides by 10: x = 90 / 10 = 9</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"0\"><p><strong>Q2.</strong> Solve for x:  x + 13 = 30</p><span class=\"rag-style-tag extreme\">Exam-style from Extreme Mathematics</span><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 159</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 17</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 16</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 19</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 20</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: A</strong> — Subtract 13 from both sides: x = 30 - 13 = 17</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"3\"><p><strong>Q3.</strong> Solve for x:  7x = 91</p><span class=\"rag-style-tag extreme\">Exam-style from Extreme Mathematics</span><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 159</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 98</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 12</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 14</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 13</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: D</strong> — Divide both sides by 7: x = 91 / 7 = 13</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"0\"><p><strong>Q4.</strong> Solve for x:  10x = 30</p><span class=\"rag-style-tag grade\">Foundational — Grade Textbook</span><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 159</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 3</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 2</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 4</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 40</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: A</strong> — Divide both sides by 10: x = 30 / 10 = 3</div></div></div>','Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 159 — Unit 3: Solving Equations Factorization Method 2 Solve the quadratic equation 𝑥2 + 6𝑥+ 9 = 0','Approved','2026-05-25 11:06:32','grade9_math.pdf',159,NULL,0,0),(73,1,'Practice: Algebra','<div class=\"rag-explanation\"><h3>Curriculum Overview</h3><p>Unit 2: The Number System 2.2.2  Conversion of repeating decimal