11</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 12</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: C</strong> — Divide both sides by 10: x = 110 / 10 = 11</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"0\"><p><strong>Q3.</strong> Find the roots of:  x² - 8x + 15 = 0</p><span class=\"rag-style-tag extreme\">Exam-style from Extreme Mathematics</span><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 61</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. x = 5 and x = 3</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. x = 6 and x = 4</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. x = -5 and x = -3</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. x = 15 and x = 8</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: A</strong> — Factor: (x - 5)(x - 3) = 0  →  x = 5 or x = 3</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"2\"><p><strong>Q4.</strong> Solve for x:  12x = 120</p><span class=\"rag-style-tag grade\">Foundational — Grade Textbook</span><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 61</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 132</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 9</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 10</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 11</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: C</strong> — Divide both sides by 12: x = 120 / 12 = 10</div></div></div>','Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 61 — Unit 2: The Number System 2.2.2  Conversion of repeating decimals into fractions','Approved','2026-05-25 11:12:13','grade9_math.pdf',61,NULL,0,0),(74,1,'Practice: Algebra','<div class=\"rag-explanation\"><h3>Curriculum Overview</h3><p>Unit 2: The Number System 2.2.2  Conversion of repeating decimals into fractions \nIn section 2.2.1, you have discussed how to convert the terminating decimals into \nfractions. In this s