lass=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: A</strong> — Add equations: 2x = 8  →  x = 4;  then y = 10 - 4 = 6</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"3\"><p><strong>Q2.</strong> Find the roots of:  x² - 9x + 20 = 0</p><span class=\"rag-style-tag extreme\">Exam-style from Extreme Mathematics</span><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 168</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. x = 6 and x = 5</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. x = -5 and x = -4</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. x = 20 and x = 9</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. x = 5 and x = 4</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: D</strong> — Factor: (x - 5)(x - 4) = 0  →  x = 5 or x = 4</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"0\"><p><strong>Q3.</strong> Solve for x:  x + 16 = 35</p><span class=\"rag-style-tag extreme\">Exam-style from Extreme Mathematics</span><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 168</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 19</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 16</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 20</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 21</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: A</strong> — Subtract 16 from both sides: x = 35 - 16 = 19</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"2\"><p><strong>Q4.</strong> Find the roots of:  x² - 6x + 8 = 0</p><span class=\"rag-style-tag grade\">Foundational — Grade Textbook</span><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 168</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. x = 5 and x = 3</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. x = -4 and x = -2</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. x = 4 and x = 2</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. x = 8 and x = 6</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: C</strong> — Factor: (x - 4)(x - 2) = 0  →  x = 4 or x = 2</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"1\"><p><strong>Q5.</strong> Solve for x:  x + 4 = 31</p><span class=\"rag-style-tag grade\">Foundational — Grade Textbook</span><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 168</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 24</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 27</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 25</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 26</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: B</strong> — Subtract 4 from both sides: x = 31 - 4 = 27</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"0\"><p><strong>Q6.</strong> Solve the system:  x + y = 8  and  x - y = -6</p><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Ethiopian Grade 10 Mathematics Textbook, page 46</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. x = 1, y = 7</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. x = 7, y = 1</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. x = 2, y = 6</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. x = 8, y = -6</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: A</strong> — Add equations: 2x = 2  →  x = 1;  then y = 8 - 1 = 7</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"2\"><p><strong>Q7.</strong> Solve for x:  x + 5 = 7</p><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Ethiopian Grade 10 Mathematics Textbook, page 46</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 0</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 1</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 2</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 3</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: C</strong> — Subtract 5 from both sides: x = 7 - 5 = 2</div></div></div>','Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 168 — Unit 4: Solving Inequalities 2. Solve the following linear inequalities.','Approved','2026-05-25 16:05:09','grade9_math.pdf',168,9,0,0),(91,1,'Practice: Algebra','<div class=\"rag-explanation\"><h3>Curriculum Overview</h3><p>A set is a collection of well-defined objects or elements. When we say a set is \nwell-defined, we mean that given an object we are able to determine whether the \nobject is in the set or not. Sets can be described in the following ways: \nVerbal method (Statement form) \nIn this method, the well-defined description of the elements of the set is written \nin an ordinary English language statement form (in words).</p></div>\n<div class=\"rag-formulas\"><h3>Key Formulas</h3><ul><li><code>identical elements. Mathematically, we write this as 𝐴= 𝐵.</code></li><li><code>1.    𝑓(𝑥) ∙𝑔(𝑥)  = (2𝑥+ 3)( 3𝑥2 −5𝑥+ 6)</code></li><li><code>= 2𝑥( 3𝑥2 −5𝑥+ 6) + 3( 3𝑥2 −5𝑥+ 6)  (Distributive property)</code></li><li><code>= ( 2𝑥)(3𝑥2) + (2𝑥)(−5𝑥) + (2𝑥)(6) + (3)(3𝑥2) + (3)(−5𝑥) + (3)(6)</code></li><li><code>= 6𝑥3 −10𝑥2 + 12𝑥+ 9𝑥2 −15𝑥+ 18</code></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"rag-examples\"><h3>Worked Examples from Textbook</h3><ul><li>c. 180, 270, 1,080 Example 2 Exercise 2.6 41</li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"rag-questions\"><h3>Practice Questions</h3><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"3\"><p><strong>Q1.</strong> Solve the system:  x + y = 9  and  x - y = -7</p><span class=\"rag-style-tag extreme\">Exam-style from Extreme Mathematics</span><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 33</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. x = 8, y = 1</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. x = 2, y = 7</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. x = 9, y = -7</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. x = 1, y = 8</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: D</strong> — Add equations: 2x = 2  →  x = 1;  then y = 9 - 1 = 8</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"1\"><p><strong>Q2.</strong> Solve for x:  x + 14 = 41</p><span class=\"rag-style-tag extreme\">Exam-style from Extreme Mathematics</span><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 33</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 24</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 27</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 26</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 28</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: B</strong> — Subtract 14 from both sides: x = 41 - 14 = 27</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"2\"><p><strong>Q3.</strong> Solve the system:  x + y = 11  and  x - y = -7</p><span class=\"rag-style-tag extreme\">Exam-style from Extreme Mathematics</span><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 33</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. x = 9, y = 2</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. x = 3, y = 8</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. x = 2, y = 9</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. x = 11, y = -7</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: C</strong> — Add equations: 2x = 4  →  x = 2;  then y = 11 - 2 = 9</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"0\"><p><strong>Q4.</strong> Solve for x:  x + 3 = 31</p><span class=\"rag-style-tag grade\">Foundational — Grade Textbook</span><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 33</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 28</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 25</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 26</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 30</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: A</strong> — Subtract 3 from both sides: x = 31 - 3 = 28</div></div></div>','Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 33 — Unit 2: Polynomial Functions 79','Approved','2026-05-25 17:56:56','grade9_math.pdf',33,9,0,0),(92,1,'Practice: Algebra','<div class=\"rag-explanation\"><h3>Curriculum Overview</h3><p>Unit 2: Polynomial Functions 79 \nc. Is the degree of 𝑓∙𝑔 equal to the sum of the degrees of 𝑓 and 𝑔? 𝑓(𝑥) ∙𝑔(𝑥)  = (2𝑥+ 3)( 3𝑥2 −5𝑥+ 6) \n                 = 2𝑥( 3𝑥2 −5𝑥+ 6) + 3( 3𝑥2 −5𝑥+ 6)  (Distributive property) \n                 = ( 2𝑥)(3𝑥2) + (2𝑥)(−5𝑥) + (2𝑥)(6) + (3)(3𝑥2) + (3)(−5𝑥) + (3)(6)          \n                       (Distributive property)                                         \n                  = 6𝑥3 −10𝑥2 + 12𝑥+ 9𝑥2 −15𝑥+ 18 \n                  = 6𝑥3 + (−10𝑥2 + 9𝑥2) + (12𝑥−15𝑥) + 18 \n                  = 6𝑥3 −𝑥2 −3𝑥+ 18 \n    2.</p></div>\n<div class=\"rag-formulas\"><h3>Key Formulas</h3><ul><li><code>1.    𝑓(𝑥) ∙𝑔(𝑥)  = (2𝑥+ 3)( 3𝑥2 −5𝑥+ 6)</code></li><li><code>= 2𝑥( 3𝑥2 −5𝑥+ 6) + 3( 3𝑥2 −5𝑥+ 6)  (Distributive property)</code></li><li><code>= ( 2𝑥)(3𝑥2) + (2𝑥)(−5𝑥) + (2𝑥)(6) + (3)(3𝑥2) + (3)(−5𝑥) + (3)(6)</code></li><li><code>= 6𝑥3 −10𝑥2 + 12𝑥+ 9𝑥2 −15𝑥+ 18</code></li><li><code>= 6𝑥3 + (−10𝑥2 + 9𝑥2) + (12𝑥−15𝑥) + 18</code></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"rag-examples\"><h3>Worked Examples from Textbook</h3><ul><li>c. 180, 270, 1,080 Example 2 Exercise 2.6 41</li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"rag-questions\"><h3>Practice Questions</h3><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"2\"><p><strong>Q1.</strong> Solve for x:  x + 11 = 26</p><span class=\"rag-style-tag extreme\">Exam-style from Extreme Mathematics</span><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 33</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 16</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 13</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 15</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 14</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: C</strong> — Subtract 11 from both sides: x = 26 - 11 = 15</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"3\"><p><strong>Q2.</strong> Find the roots of:  x² - 6x + 8 = 0</p><span class=\"rag-style-tag extreme\">Exam-style from Extreme Mathematics</span><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 33</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. x = 5 and x = 3</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. x = -4 and x = -2</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. x = 8 and x = 6</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. x = 4 and x = 2</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: D</strong> — Factor: (x - 4)(x - 2) = 0  →  x = 4 or x = 2</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"0\"><p><strong>Q3.</strong> Solve for x:  8x = 96</p><span class=\"rag-style-tag extreme\">Exam-style from Extreme Mathematics</span><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 33</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 12</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 104</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 11</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 13</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: A</strong> — Divide both sides by 8: x = 96 / 8 = 12</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"1\"><p><strong>Q4.</strong> Solve for x:  6x = 24</p><span class=\"rag-style-tag grade\">Foundational — Grade Textbook</span><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 33</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 3</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 4</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 5</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 10</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: B</strong> — Divide both sides by 6: x = 24 / 6 = 4</div></div></div>','Ethiopian Grade 10 Mathematic