trong> Use these standard methods for Algebra: factorization method.</li><li class=\"rag-step-item\"><strong>Step 3:</strong> Key formula to remember: c) Find p such that log6 6 = p. d) Simplify 2log2 3p. Laws of logarithms</li><li class=\"rag-step-item\"><strong>Step 4:</strong> Also useful: Let logaM= p and logaN= q.</li><li class=\"rag-step-item\"><strong>Step 5:</strong> Practice with similar problems and check each step before moving on.</li><li class=\"rag-step-item\"><strong>Step 6:</strong> Verify your final answer by substituting back or using a quick estimate.</li></ol></div>\n<div class=\"rag-formulas\"><h3>Key Formulas</h3><ul><li><code>c) Find p such that log6 6 = p. d) Simplify 2log2 3p. Laws of logarithms</code></li><li><code>Let logaM= p and logaN= q.</code></li><li><code>Converting to exponential equations, we get : ap= M and aq= N.</code></li><li><code>Now, MN= ap∙ aq= ap+q.</code></li><li><code>This implies MN= ap+q.</code></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"rag-examples\"><h3>Curriculum Examples</h3><ul><li><p>c) Find p such that log6 6 = p. d) Simplify 2log2 3p. Laws of logarithms</p></li><li><p>a) Find p such that log2 p= log2 5. b) Simplify log2 2p.</p></li><li><p>c) Find p such that log3 3 = p. d) Simplify 5log5 p.</p></li><li><p>a) Find p such that log3 p= log3 4. b) Simplify log5 25p.</p></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"rag-questions\"><h3>Practice Questions</h3><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"1\"><p><strong>Q1.</strong> Solve the system: x + y = 9 and x - y = 3</p><span class=\"rag-style-tag extreme\">Exam-style from Extreme Mathematics</span><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 35</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. x = 3, y = 6</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. x = 6, y = 3</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. x = 7, y = 2</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. x = 9, y = 3</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: B</strong> — Add equations: 2x = 12 → x = 6; then y = 9 - 6 = 3</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"1\"><p><strong>Q2.</strong> Find the roots of: x² - 4x + 3 = 0</p><span class=\"rag-style-tag extreme\">Exam-style from Extreme Mathematics</span><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 35</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. x = 2 and x = 4</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. x = 1 and x = 3</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. x = -1 and x = -3</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. x = 3 and x = 4</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: B</strong> — Factor: (x - 1)(x - 3) = 0 → x = 1 or x = 3</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"1\"><p><strong>Q3.</strong> Solve the system: x + y = 15 and x - y = -1</p><span class=\"rag-style-tag extreme\">Exam-style from Extreme Mathematics</span><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 35</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. x = 8, y = 7</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. x = 7, y = 8</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. x = 8, y = 7</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. x = 15, y = -1</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: B</strong> — Add equations: 2x = 14 → x = 7; then y = 15 - 7 = 8</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"1\"><p><strong>Q4.</strong> Solve for x: x + 4 = 26</p><span class=\"rag-style-tag grade\">Foundational — Grade Textbook</span><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 35</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 25</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 22</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 19</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 28</li></ul><div clas