et (⊂) Definition 1.5 Set A is said to be a subset of set B if every element of A is also an element of B. Figure 1.3 shows this relationship. Mathematically, we write this as 𝑨 ⊆ 𝑩. If set A is not a subset of set B, then it is written as A ⊈ B. Example 4 i) Any set is a subset of itself. ii) Empty set is a subset of every set. iii) If set A is finite with n elements, then the number of subsets of set A is 2n. Note Definition 1.6 If A⊆B and A≠B, then A is called the proper subset of set B and it can be written as A⊂B. Figure 1.3</p></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"rag-questions\"><h3>Practice Questions</h3><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"2\"><p><strong>Q1.</strong> A survey of 46 students found 29 study Math and 12 study Science. 5 study both, and 8 study neither. How many study Math ONLY?</p><span class=\"rag-style-tag extreme\">Exam-style from Extreme Mathematics</span><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 21</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 17</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 5</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 24</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 12</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: C</strong> — Math only = n(Math) - n(Math∩Science) = 29 - 5 = 24</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"1\"><p><strong>Q2.</strong> A survey of 20 students found 6 study Math and 13 study Science. 5 study both, and 6 study neither. How many study Math ONLY?</p><span class=\"rag-style-tag extreme\">Exam-style from Extreme Mathematics</span><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 21</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 5</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 1</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 13</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 14</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none