\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: D</strong> — Divide both sides by 8: x = 32 / 8 = 4</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"1\"><p><strong>Q2.</strong> Solve the system: x + y = 7 and x - y = -1</p><span class=\"rag-style-tag extreme\">Exam-style from Extreme Mathematics</span><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 158</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. x = 4, y = 3</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. x = 3, y = 4</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. x = 4, y = 3</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. x = 7, y = -1</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: B</strong> — Add equations: 2x = 6 → x = 3; then y = 7 - 3 = 4</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"0\"><p><strong>Q3.</strong> Solve the system: x + y = 9 and x - y = 1</p><span class=\"rag-style-tag extreme\">Exam-style from Extreme Mathematics</span><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 158</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. x = 5, y = 4</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. x = 4, y = 5</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. x = 6, y = 3</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. x = 9, y = 1</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: A</strong> — Add equations: 2x = 10 → x = 5; then y = 9 - 5 = 4</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"0\"><p><strong>Q4.</strong> Solve for x: 4x = 16</p><span class=\"rag-style-tag grade\">Foundational — Grade Textbook</span><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 158</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 4</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 3</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 5</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 8</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: A</strong> — Divide both sides by 4: x = 16 / 4 = 4</div></div></div>','Ethiopian Grade 10 Mathematics Textbook, page 43 — Unit 1: Relations and Functions 34 That is, the graph of 𝑓 is the set of all points ( ,  ) such that 𝑓( ) =  . This is the','Pending','2026-05-27 21:31:30','grade10_math.pdf',43,9,0,0),(127,2,'Practice: Limits','<div class=\"rag-explanation\"><h3>Curriculum Overview</h3><p>Unit 9: Statistics and Probability Steps in drawing a histogram Label the marks so that the scale is clear and give a name to the x- axis. Choose a scale for the vertical axis that will accommodate the class with the \nhighest frequency.</p></div>\n<div class=\"rag-steps\"><h3>Step-by-Step Guide</h3><ol class=\"rag-step-list\"><li class=\"rag-step-item\"><strong>Step 1:</strong> Start with the overview above, then apply these steps for Limits: Unit 9: Statistics and Probability Steps in drawing a histogram Label the marks so that the scale is clear and give a name to the x- axis.</li><li class=\"rag-step-item\"><strong>Step 2:</strong> Key formula to remember: 25 ≤s&lt; 30</li><li class=\"rag-step-item\"><strong>Step 3:</strong> Also useful: 30 ≤s&lt; 35</li><li class=\"rag-step-item\"><strong>Step 4:</strong> Practice with similar problems and check each step before moving on.</li><li class=\"rag-step-item\"><strong>Step 5:</strong> Verify your final answer by substituting back or using a quick estimate.</li></ol></div>\n<div class=\"rag-formulas\"><h3>Key Formulas</h3><ul><li><code>25 ≤s&lt; 30</code></li><li><code>30 ≤s&lt; 35</code></li><li><code>35 ≤s&lt; 40</code></li><li><code>40 ≤s&lt; 45</code></li><li><code>45 ≤s&lt; 50</code></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"rag-questions\"><h3>Practice Questions</h3><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"3\"><p><strong>Q1.</strong> Evaluate: lim(x → 3) (x + 8)</p><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Curriculum Source</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 3</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 8</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 10</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 11</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: D</strong> — Direct substitution: 3 + 8 = 11</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"3\"><p><strong>Q2.</strong> Evaluate: lim(x → 4) (x + 5)</p><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Curriculum Source</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 4</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 5</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 8</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 9</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: D</strong> — Direct substitution: 4 + 5 = 9</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"3\"><p><strong>Q3.</strong> Evaluate: lim(x → 7) (x + 10)</p><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Curriculum Source</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 7</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 10</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 16</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 17</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: D</strong> — Direct substitution: 7 + 10 = 17</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"2\"><p><strong>Q4.</strong> Evaluate: lim(x → ∞) (4x + 4) / (3x + 5)</p><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Curriculum Source</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. 5/3</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. 1</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. 4/3</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. 4/5</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: C</strong> — Divide numerator and denominator by x: limit = 4/3 = 4/3</div></div></div>','Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 336 — Unit 9: Statistics and Probability Steps in drawing a histogram','Approved','2026-05-27 22:15:03','grade9_math.pdf',336,9,0,0),(128,7,'Practice: Quadratic Equation','<div class=\"rag-explanation\"><h3>Curriculum Overview</h3><p>Unit 1: Relations and Functions 41 Sketch the graph of each of the following using intercepts: \na. = −4 + 3 Graphs of quadratic functions \nA function defined by f( ) = a 2 + b + c where a, b, c are real numbers and a≠\n0 is called a quadratic function. Use graphical method to solve the following.</p></div>\n<div class=\"rag-steps\"><h3>Step-by-Step Guide</h3><ol class=\"rag-step-list\"><li class=\"rag-step-item\"><strong>Step 1:</strong> Start with the overview above, then apply these steps for Quadratic Equation: Unit 1: Relations and Functions 41 Sketch the graph of each of the following using intercepts: \na.</li><li class=\"rag-step-item\"><strong>Step 2:</strong> Use these standard methods for Quadratic Equation: Factorization method, completing the square, quadratic formula.</li><li class=\"rag-step-item\"><strong>Step 3:</strong> Key formula to remember: b = c = 0.</li><li class=\"rag-step-item\"><strong>Step 4:</strong> Also useful: a. 2 −1 = 0 b. 2 + 2 + 1 = 0</li><li class=\"rag-step-item\"><strong>Step 5:</strong> Follow this worked example from your textbook: stretching/ shrinking and shifting (translation) the parabola = 2. Example 1 The simplest form of a quadratic equation is = 2 when a = 1 and b = c = 0. Note a. Make a table of ordered pairs that satisfy the function f( ) = 2. b. Find the and intercepts of f. c. Plot the points ( , 2) on -coordinate system. d. Find the domain and range of f. Activity 1.9</li><li class=\"rag-step-item\"><strong>Step 6:</strong> Verify your final answer by substituting back or using a quick estimate.</li></ol></div>\n<div class=\"rag-formulas\"><h3>Key Formulas</h3><ul><li><code>b = c = 0.</code></li><li><code>a. 2 −1 = 0 b. 2 + 2 + 1 = 0</code></li><li><code>c. 2 + 3 −4 = 0 d. 2 −4 + 6 = 0</code></li><li><code>What is the solution set of the equation f( ) = 0?</code></li><li><code>the graph opens up or down. If a&gt; 0, then the graph opens up and if a&lt; 0, then</code></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"rag-examples\"><h3>Worked Examples from Textbook</h3><ul><li><p>stretching/ shrinking and shifting (translation) the parabola = 2. Example 1 The simplest form of a quadratic equation is = 2 when a = 1 and b = c = 0. Note a. Make a table of ordered pairs that satisfy the function f( ) = 2. b. Find the and intercepts of f. c. Plot the points ( , 2) on -coordinate system. d. Find the domain and range of f. Activity 1.9</p></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"rag-questions\"><h3>Practice Questions</h3><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"2\"><p><strong>Q1.</strong> Find the roots of: x² - 6x + 8 = 0</p><span class=\"rag-style-tag extreme\">Exam-style from Extreme Mathematics</span><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 159</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. x = 5 and x = 3</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. x = -4 and x = -2</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. x = 4 and x = 2</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. x = 8 and x = 6</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: C</strong> — Factor: (x - 4)(x - 2) = 0 → x = 4 or x = 2</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"3\"><p><strong>Q2.</strong> Solve the system: x + y = 14 and x - y = 0</p><span class=\"rag-style-tag extreme\">Exam-style from Extreme Mathematics</span><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 159</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. x = 7, y = 7</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. x = 8, y = 6</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. x = 14, y = 0</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. x = 7, y = 7</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: D</strong> — Add equations: 2x = 14 → x = 7; then y = 14 - 7 = 7</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"0\"><p><strong>Q3.</strong> Solve the system: x + y = 10 and x - y = -6</p><span class=\"rag-style-tag extreme\">Exam-style from Extreme Mathematics</span><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 159</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. x = 2, y = 8</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. x = 8, y = 2</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. x = 3, y = 7</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. x = 10, y = -6</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: A</strong> — Add equations: 2x = 4 → x = 2; then y = 10 - 2 = 8</div></div><div class=\"rag-question\" data-correct=\"3\"><p><strong>Q4.</strong> Find the roots of: x² - 13x + 42 = 0</p><span class=\"rag-style-tag grade\">Foundational — Grade Textbook</span><span class=\"rag-src-tag\">Source: Ethiopian Grade 9 Mathematics Textbook, page 159</span><ul class=\"rag-options\"><li data-idx=\"0\" class=\"rag-option\">A. x = 7 and x = 8</li><li data-idx=\"1\" class=\"rag-option\">B. x = -6 and x = -7</li><li data-idx=\"2\" class=\"rag-option\">C. x = 42 and x = 13</li><li data-idx=\"3\" class=\"rag-option\">D. x = 6 and x = 7</li></ul><div class=\"rag-answer\" style=\"display:none\"><strong>Answer: D</strong> — Factor: (x - 6)(x - 7) = 0 → x = 6 or x = 7</div></div></div>','Ethiopian Grade 10 Mathematics Textbook, page 50 — Unit 1: Relations and Functions 41','Approved','2026-05-28 11:40:57','grade10_math.pdf',50,9,0,0);
